    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded disposable-email-domain rejection with minimal structural impact:\n\n- **New file** `DisposableEmailDomains.java` \u2014 a small, cohesive helper (one static `reject` method, WMC_other \u2248 0) that extracts the email domain and calls `errors.rejectValue(...)` when it's on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). This mirrors the existing `E164Telephone`/`AddressNormalizer` helper pattern in the same package.\n- **One-line edit** in `OwnerFieldsValidator.validate` \u2014 a single delegating call `DisposableEmailDomains.reject(owner.getEmail(), errors);` placed right after the existing email normalization, so `validate`'s own cyclomatic complexity is unchanged and only one line was touched in that class.\n\nRejections in the validator surface as HTTP 400, satisfying the spec. `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite are green.",
